4. PER-KEY JUDGEMENT (vi)
-------------------------
4.1 ui.chat.composer_media.pasted_image = "Ảnh đã dán"  ("Pasted image")
    Fallback filename/caption for an image data URI with no usable encoded name.
    - Parallel to the existing pasted_file "Tệp đã dán" and pasted_type
      "Đã dán {mimeType}": same participial shape, no extension, no MIME prose,
      which the sidecar requires ("No file extension, MIME identifier or
      placeholder is part of this message.").
    - Short form "Ảnh" is the catalogue's compact-attachment register:
      ui.canvas.files.attachmentImage "Ảnh đính kèm", ui.agents.avatar
      "Ảnh đại diện", ui.common.viewer.image_progress "Ảnh {index} / {count}".
      "Hình ảnh" exists too, but as the category/noun label
      (ui.canvas.files.images "Hình ảnh", ui.chat.canonical.image_label
      "Hình ảnh") and would be longer and less parallel here. No finding.
    - NFC: Ả is U+1EA2 precomposed (E8). Style guide NFC rule satisfied.

4.2 ui.chat.image_actions.actions = "Thao tác với ảnh"  ("Image actions")
    Default tooltip + unnamed-image accessible-name fallback.
    - Byte-identical to two existing values for the same concept:
      ui.canvas.files.imageActions "Thao tác với ảnh" and
      ui.canvas.finder_files_view.ui_canvas_files_imageactions "Thao tác với ảnh";
      and it parallels ui.common.actions.file_actions_menu.file_actions
      "Thao tác với tệp" and ui.canvas.files.fileActions "Thao tác với tệp".
    - The code confirms the shape is right: ImageActionsMenu's unnamed fallback
      (image-actions-menu.tsx) now resolves to this key while the named path
      resolves to actions_for_name, so "Thao tác với ảnh" / "Thao tác với tệp" /
      "Thao tác với <tên>" form one paradigm. No finding.

4.3 ui.chat.audio.position_label = "Vị trí phát của {label}"  ("{label} position")
    Accessible name of the clip's seek slider (sound-player.tsx line 455,
    aria-label on the slider).
    - Term: "Vị trí phát" is the catalogue's established rendering of playback
      position — ui.chat.attachments.playback_position "Vị trí phát". Reusing it
      is required consistency, not a choice.
    - "của" is grammatically necessary: "Vị trí phát {label}" would read as a
      mis-ordered compound. Neighbouring audio keys are verb-first
      ("Phát {label}", "Tạm dừng {label}") and correctly have no "của" because a
      verb governs its object directly; a noun phrase needs the possessive. This
      is agreement with the key's own grammar, not a divergence from the
      play/pause labels.
    - Arbitrary inserted text: no case/gender/number agreement exists in
      Vietnamese, so any file name, Latin title, CJK title, quoted name or name
      ending in punctuation stays grammatical after "của". The sidecar explicitly
      allows the word order used ("Word order may change around {label}").
    - Rejected candidate for a NIT: if a future label itself contained a
      "… của X" phrase the sentence would read "…của … của …". Not raised: labels
      here are media display titles/filenames (canonical-audio.tsx and
      supplement-row.tsx pass the clip label straight through), the English has
      the same dependency on the inserted string, and any alternative
      ("Vị trí phát: {label}", "{label} — vị trí phát") trades this improbable
      clumsiness for a real ambiguity about whether the string names the slider
      or its value. Nothing in the catalogue or the style guide backs a change.

4.4 ui.common.actions.actions_for_name = "Thao tác với {name}"  ("Actions for {name}")
    Shared file/image overflow-menu accessible name for a named asset.
    - Byte-identical to the existing value of the same shape:
      ui.chat.canonical.link_toolkit.actions_for "Thao tác với {name}".
    - The catalogue also carries "Thao tác cho {name}" in four legacy keys
      (ui.projects.project_board.actions_for_displayname, ui.shell
      .sidebar_navigation.row_actions, ui.library.menu.asset_actions_label,
      ui.settings.appearance.editor.more). Both prepositions are grammatical;
      the translator chose the variant that already exists verbatim for the same
      English pattern, which is the stronger consistency call. A change to "cho"
      would break exact parity with link_toolkit.actions_for. No finding; the
      legacy split is a pre-existing inconsistency outside this delta.
    - Placeholder: {name} byte-exact, plain, single, no ICU. Verbatim insertion
      of a user file name keeps the sentence grammatical; the code inserts the
      label/name unchanged (supplement-file-actions.tsx, image-actions-menu.tsx)
      and the unnamed file path correctly falls back to "Thao tác với tệp".

