6. CONTEXT-METADATA ACCURACY (English, in scope)
------------------------------------------------
Checked the broadened ui.chat.composer_media.pasted_file note sentence:
"Fallback for non-image data URIs with no usable name, including invalid percent
encoding, whether or not a MIME type is present. Also used as synthetic upload
metadata; valid names and attachment bytes stay unchanged."
Against get-file-name.ts: `data:image/` branch returns pasted_image (missing
name= or a throwing decodeURIComponent), the later `data:` branch returns
pasted_file for everything else with the same name/decode test — so "non-image
data URIs", "no usable name", "invalid percent encoding" and "whether or not a
MIME type is present" are all accurate. Against attachment-encode.ts: the value
becomes the upload source's `name` (`{ kind: "dataUrl", dataUrl, name }`) and the
wire file entry's name (`stored.name ?? name`), while the original dataUrl is
passed untouched — so "Also used as synthetic upload metadata" and "valid names
and attachment bytes stay unchanged" are accurate too. A pedantic residue exists
(a data URI written with an upper-case scheme/`DATA:IMAGE/` would fall through to
pasted_file) but that behaviour pre-dates this PR, is unchanged by it, and does
not falsify the sentence's intent. No finding.
The new pasted_image note was checked the same way and matches the code.
The two new accessor notes (image_actions.actions, actions_for_name) match their
call sites exactly, including "a named image instead uses
ui.common.actions.actions_for_name" and the caller-override reservation.

